WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.941
The takeaway is simple: instead of exchanging raw
sensitive data,

00:00:04.021 --> 00:00:09.570
collaborating organizations can share the
latent-space embeddings produced by autoencoders.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:14.766
This keeps the original features private yet
preserves most of the predictive power,

00:00:14.846 --> 00:00:20.024
with performance dropping by less than ten
percentage points across three benchmarks.

00:00:20.104 --> 00:00:25.035
Making the autoencoder aware of the downstream task
narrows the gap even further.

00:00:25.115 --> 00:00:30.726
The authors point to custom per-dataset
autoencoders and formal measures of privacy strength

00:00:30.806 --> 00:00:35.180
as the next steps toward deploying this in real
organizational settings.
